nsactivation domain (AD; amino acids 300–655) of ASXL1, newly defined in this study, interacts with the C-terminal AD2 (amino acids 1217–1441) of SRC-1, suggesting that one AD cooperates with the other AD in transcriptional activation by RAR."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":157,"s":102,"t":53,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16239140"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0004730"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["irozzo"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16239140\">pubmed:16239140</a> We demonstrate here that oncogenic MLL fusion proteins retain an ability to stably associate with menin through a high-affinity, amino-terminal, conserved binding motif and that this interaction is required for the initiation of MLL-mediated leukemogenesis.These results demonstrate that a human oncoprotein is critically dependent on direct physical interaction with a tumor suppressor protein for its oncogenic activity[...]."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":158,"s":102,"t":52,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16239140"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0004730"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["irozzo"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16239140\">pubmed:16239140</a> We demonstrate here that oncogenic MLL fusion proteins retain an ability to stably associate with menin through a high-affinity, amino-terminal, conserved binding motif and that this interaction is required for the initiation of MLL-mediated leukemogenesis.These results demonstrate that a human oncoprotein is critically dependent on direct physical interaction with a tumor suppressor protein for its oncogenic activity[...]."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":159,"s":102,"t":43,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16239140"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0004730"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["irozzo"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16239140\">pubmed:16239140</a> We demonstrate here that oncogenic MLL fusion proteins retain an ability to stably associate with menin through a high-affinity, amino-terminal, conserved binding motif and that this interaction is required for the initiation of MLL-mediated leukemogenesis.These results demonstrate that a human oncoprotein is critically dependent on direct physical interaction with a tumor suppressor protein for its oncogenic activity[...]."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":160,"s":102,"t":22,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16239140"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0004730"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16239140\">pubmed:16239140</a> We demonstrate here that oncogenic MLL fusion proteins retain an ability to stably associate with menin through a high-affinity, amino-terminal, conserved binding motif and that this interaction is required for the initiation of MLL-mediated leukemogenesis.These results demonstrate that a human oncoprotein is critically dependent on direct physical interaction with a tumor suppressor protein for its oncogenic activity."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":161,"s":102,"t":14,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16415155"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["irozzo"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16415155\">pubmed:16415155</a> We also found that menin is important for the proliferation of MLL oncoprotein-transformed myeloid cells, pointing to a paradoxically oncogenic role for the tumor suppressor menin in proliferation of transformed myeloid cells."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":162,"s":103,"t":55,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:24316979"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence