"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/21779497\">pubmed:21779497</a> The raf family of proteins (raf-1, a-raf, and b-raf) is serine/threonine kinases that bind to the effector region of ras-gtp, thus inducing translocation of the protein to the plasma membrane. Once there, raf proteins are activated and phosphorylated by different protein kinases."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":189,"s":49,"t":55,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:21779497"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/21779497\">pubmed:21779497</a> Grb2 binds and activates sos, which then activates ras, and this activates p110 independently of p85./it was also described that ras interacts with pi3k in a direct manner./lysine residue 227 is essential for the interaction of ras with pi3k"],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":192,"s":71,"t":57,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:10226025","pubmed:12808134","pubmed:15743829","pubmed:9512493","pubmed:15718470"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["","Thr308"],"sequence":["KDGATMKtFCGTPEY",""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":["","BTO:0000142","BTO:0001103","BTO:0000887","BTO:0001760"],"notes":[""],"annotator":["lperfetto","gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15718470\">pubmed:15718470</a>  Akt/PKB activation requires the phosphorylation of Thr308 in the activation loop by the phosphoinositide-dependent kinase 1 (PDK1) and Ser473 within the carboxyl-terminal hydrophobic motif by an unknown kinase.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9512493\">pubmed:9512493</a>  The activation of PKBbeta and PKBamma by PDK11 was accompanied by the phosphorylation of the residues equivalent to Thr308 in PKBalpha, namely Thr309 (PKBbeta) and Thr305 (PKBgamma)","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15743829\">pubmed:15743829</a>  3-phosphoinositide-dependent kinase 1 (PDK1) phosphorylates the activation loop of a number of protein serine/threonine kinases of the AGC kinase superfamily, including protein kinase B (PKB; also called Akt),","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10226025\">pubmed:10226025</a> Protein kinase B (PKB) is activated by phosphorylation of Thr308 and of Ser473. Thr308 is phosphorylated by the 3-phosphoinositide-dependent protein kinase-1 (PDK1) but the identity of the kinase that phosphorylates Ser473 (provisionally termed PDK2) is unknown.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12808134\">pubmed:12808134</a>  Akt1 and akt2 are phosphorylated and activated by the protein kinase pdk1 at thr-308 or thr-309, respectively, in the activation t-loop, and further activation occurs through phosphorylation at ser-473 or ser-474, respectively. In this paper, we demonstrate that this is indeed the case, and report the purification and initial characterization of a 3 phosphoinositide-dependent protein kinase, pdk1, which activates pkb by phosphorylating it at thr308. Akt is directly phosphorylated and activated by pdk1. Akt/pkb activation requires the phosphorylation of thr308 in the activation loop by the phosphoinositide-dependent kinase 1 (pdk1)."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":195,"s":61,"t":36,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:12835716"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12835716\">pubmed:12835716</a> C-myc also directly represses transcription of cdk kinase inhibitors including p27kip1, p21cip1, p15ink4b and p16ink4a"],"i":"down-regulates quantity by repression"}},{"id":196,"s":61,"t":113,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:26049753"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/26049753\">pubmed:26049753</a> USP22 expression was regulated by c-MYC and contributed to c-MYC mediated reduction in SIRT1 polyubiquitination and degradation. USP22 directly interacted with and removing polyubiquitin chains from SIRT1 to increase SIRT1 protein stabilization and expression. These results support a role for USP22 in MYC-mediated increase in SIRT1 protein stabilization, and indicate that FLT3-ITD, c-MYC and USP22 form an oncogenic network that enhances SIRT1 expression and activity in leukemic cells."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":197,"s":61,"t":14,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:9552384"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9552384\">pubmed:9552384</a> C-myc has emerged as one of the central regulators of mammalian cell proliferation."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":198,"s":114,"t":5,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:30205049"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/30205049\">pubmed:30205049</a> In AML cells, NPM1 mutations result in abnormal cytoplasmic localization of the mutant protein (NPM1c); however, it is unknown whether NPM1c is required to maintain the leukemic state. Here, we show that loss of NPM1c from the cytoplasm, either through nuclear relocalization or targeted degradation, results in immediate downregulation of homeobox (HOX) genes followed by differentiation."],"i":"down-regulates quantity by repression"}},{"id":199,"s":114,"t":115,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:18625840"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0002572"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/18625840\">pubmed:18625840</a> We report here that NPM regulates turnover of the c-Myc oncoprotein by acting on the F-box protein Fbw7 , a component of the E3 ligase complex involved in the ubiquitination and proteasome degradation of c-Myc. NPM was required for nucleolar localization and stabili- zation of Fbw7"],"i":"up-regulates quantity"}},{"id":200,"s":114,"t":36,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16199867"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16199867\">pubmed:16199867</a> The Arf-NPM interaction seems to be critical in regulating the stability of both proteins. Arf, in fact, induces polyubiquitination and degradation of NPM and inhibits its effects on ribogenesis (18). NPM, instead, protects Arf from degradation and, surprisingly, antagonizes its ability to inhibit cell division"],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":201,"s":68,"t":27,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:22337874","pubmed:10935507","pubmed:23150757"],"mechanism":["ubiquitination"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/22337874\">pubmed:22337874</a> The E3 ubiquitin ligase, MDM2, uses a dual-site mechanism to ubiquitinate and degrade the tumor suppressor protein p53, involving interactions with the N-terminal hydrophobic pocket and the acidic domain of MDM2.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10935507\">pubmed:10935507</a>  Many posttranslational modifications of p53, such as phosphorylation, dephosphorylation, acetylation and ribosylation, have been shown to occur following cellular stress. Some of these modifications may activate the p53 protein, interfere with MDM2 binding and/or dictate cellular localization of p53.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23150757\">pubmed:23150757</a>  Dual Roles of MDM2 in the Regulation of p53: Ubiquitination Dependent and Ubiquitination Independent Mechanisms of MDM2 Repression of p53 Activity"],"i":"down-regulates quantity by destabilization"}},{"id":204,"s":13,"t":70,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:29090344"],"mechanism":["chemical modification"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/29090344\">pubmed:29090344</a> Two of the most commonly mutated genes in AML encode for two isoforms of isocitrate dehydrogenase (IDH), IDH1 and IDH2. IDH1 and IDH2 are two isoforms of isocitrate dehydrogenase that perform crucial roles in cellular metabolism. Somatic mutations in either of these two genes impart a neomorphic enzymatic activity upon the encoded enzymes resulting in the ability to convert √é¬±-ketoglutarate (√é¬±KG) into the oncometabolite R2-hydroxyglutarate (R2-HG), which can competitively inhibit multiple √é¬±KG-dependent dioxygenases. "],"i":"up-regulates quantity"}},{"id":205,"s":48,"t":116,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:10570290","pubmed:23452850","pubmed:8479541"],"mechanism":["relocalization"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["","BTO:0001412","BTO:0000669"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":["GRB2 associated guanine nucleotide exchange factor Sos activates Ras through the exchange of GDP for GTP"],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23452850\">pubmed:23452850</a> Interaction domains of sos1/grb2 are finely tuned for cooperative control of embryonic stem cell fate.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10570290\">pubmed:10570290</a>  Grb2 binds and activates sos, which then activates ras, and this activates p110 independently of p85.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/8479541\">pubmed:8479541</a>  Furthermore, our results indicate that the interaction domains of sos1 and grb2 have evolved so as to bind ligands not with maximal strength but with specificities and affinities that maintain cooperativity. Grb2 binds and activates sos, which then activates ras, and this activates p110 independently of p85."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":208,"s":48,"t":117,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:11823423"],"mechanism":["relocalization"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":["GRB2 is an adapter protein that provides a critical link between cell surface growth factor receptors and the Ras signaling pathway."],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/11823423\">pubmed:11823423</a> The underlying mechanism seems to involve recruitment of a grb2 c-cbl complex to grb2-specific docking sites of egfr, and concurrent acceleration of receptor ubiquitylation and desensitization."],"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":209,"s":108,"t":101,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:1310351"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/1310351\">pubmed:1310351</a> Here we report that the transcriptional activity of rar and rxr can be reciprocally modulated by direct interactions between the two proteins"],"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":210,"s":118,"t":15,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:11907276"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["amattioni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/11907276\">pubmed:11907276</a> Caspase-3 cleaves parp-1. During cd95-mediated apoptosis proteolytic inactivation of parp-1 by caspases prevents atp depletion and thereby ensures the execution of the apoptotic process"],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates"}},{"id":211,"s":113,"t":92,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:26049753"],"mechanism":["deubiquitination"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/26049753\">pubmed:26049753</a> USP22 expression was regulated by c-MYC and contributed to c-MYC mediated reduction in SIRT1 polyubiquitination and degradation. USP22 directly interacted with and removing polyubiquitin chains from SIRT1 to increase SIRT1 protein stabilization and expression. These results support a role for USP22 in MYC-mediated increase in SIRT1 protein stabilization, and indicate that FLT3-ITD, c-MYC and USP22 form an oncogenic network that enhances SIRT1 expression and activity in leukemic cells."],"i":"up-regulates quantity by stabilization"}},{"id":212,"s":119,"t":15,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:23567751"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23567751\">pubmed:23567751</a> The mitochondrial pathway of apoptosis proceeds when the outer mitochondrial membrane (OMM) is compromised by the pro-apoptotic BCL-2 family members, BAK and BAX. Once activated, BAK and BAX form proteolipid pores in the OMM leading to mitochondrial outer membrane permeabilization (MOMP), and the release of inner membrane space proteins, such as cytochrome c, which promotes caspase activation."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":213,"s":120,"t":121,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:27096005"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["areggio"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/27096005\">pubmed:27096005</a> Through study of FZD4 and its associated ligand Norrin, we report that a minimum of three residues distal to the KTXXXW motif in the C-terminal tail of Frizzled-4 are essential for DVL recruitment and robust Lef/Tcf-dependent transcriptional activation in response to Norrin."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":214,"s":111,"t":14,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:26728554"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":["BTO:0000089"],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/26728554\">pubmed:26728554</a> Hhex is a potential therapeutic target that is specifically required for AML stem cells to repress tumor suppressor pathways and enable continued self-renewal."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":215,"s":10,"t":90,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:14982881"],"mechanism":["relocalization"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/14982881\">pubmed:14982881</a> We report here that the Flt3-ITD interferes with the transcriptional and biologic action of the PLZF transcriptional repressor. In the presence of Flt3-ITD, PLZF-SMRT interaction was reduced, transcriptional repression by PLZF was inhibited, and PLZF-mediated growth suppression of leukemia cells was partially blocked. Furthermore, overexpression of Flt3-ITD led to a partial relocalization of SMRT protein from the nucleus to the cytoplasm."],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates activity"}},{"id":216,"s":10,"t":122,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:23246379"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0001516"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23246379\">pubmed:23246379</a> These results suggest that Grb10 binds to both normal and oncogenic FLT3 and induces PI3K–Akt and STAT5 signaling pathways resulting in an enhanced proliferation, survival and colony formation of hematopoietic cells."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":217,"s":10,"t":29,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16146838","pubmed:14592841"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["","lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/14592841\">pubmed:14592841</a>  Thus, induction of C/EBPα and PU.1 expression is inhibited in 32D cells due to the expression of FLT3/ITD","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16146838\">pubmed:16146838</a> Oncogenic mutations of Flt3 also result in the activation of aberrant signaling pathways, including strong activation of STAT5, induction of STAT target genes, and repression of myeloid transcription factors c/EBP-3 and Pu.1."],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates quantity by repression"}},{"id":219,"s":10,"t":123,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:15769897","pubmed:10482988"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr349","Tyr350","Tyr427",""],"sequence":["","EEPPDHQyYNDFPGK","ELFDDPSyVNVQNLD","EPPDHQYyNDFPGKE"],"cell_data":["","BTO:0002882"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["","miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15769897\">pubmed:15769897</a>   we observed constitutive activation of Erk-1 and Erk-2, Akt, and of Shc by both Flt3-ITD and Flt3-D835Y","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10482988\">pubmed:10482988</a>  Intracellular FLT3 signaling involves tyrosine phosphorylation of several cytoplasmic proteins including SHC. We have found that upon FLT3 activation SHC phosphorylation occurs at tyrosine 239/240 and 313. ","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10482988\">pubmed:10482988</a> Intracellular FLT3 signaling involves tyrosine phosphorylation of several cytoplasmic proteins including SHC. We have found that upon FLT3 activation SHC phosphorylation occurs at tyrosine 239/240 and 313. "],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":223,"s":10,"t":42,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:17851558"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0001545"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/17851558\">pubmed:17851558</a> Endogenous beta-catenin co-immunoprecipitated with endogenous activated FLT3, and recombinant activated FLT3 directly phosphorylated recombinant beta-catenin. Finally, FLT3 inhibitor decreased tyrosine phosphorylation of beta-catenin in leukemia cells obtained from FLT3-ITD-positive AML patients. These data demonstrate that FLT3 activation induces beta-catenin tyrosine phosphorylation and nuclear localization, and thus suggest a mechanism for the association of FLT3 activation and beta-catenin oncogeneic signaling in AML."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":224,"s":10,"t":21,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:18559972"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["apalma"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/18559972\">pubmed:18559972</a> In this study, we used specific tyrosine kinase inhibitors to identify critical target genes that are regulated by oncogenic tyrosine kinases. Using oligonucleotide microarrays, we identified genes that are either up- or down-regulated by selective small molecule inhibitors that target the ABL, PDGFβR, or FLT3 kinases. Genes induced by these inhibitors are presumably repressed by activated tyrosine kinases.Among these genes, we detected a 5- to 50-fold reduction in Id1 expression when the cancer cells were treated with inhibitors."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":225,"s":10,"t":120,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:15650056"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0002882"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15650056\">pubmed:15650056</a> AML-typical Flt3 mutations induce the expression of Frizzled-4 on the mRNA and protein level, mimicking the effects of IL-3."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":226,"s":10,"t":118,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:21228325"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/21228325\">pubmed:21228325</a> Interestingly, quantitative RT-PCR analysis demonstrated a 2-fold increase in PARP-1 expression. Western blotting analysis of protein nuclear extracts from FLT3/ITD B-cells confirmed that PARP1 was up-regulated, compared with wild-type controls "],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":227,"s":10,"t":48,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:10080542"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10080542\">pubmed:10080542</a> FL stimulation induces association of Grb2 with Flt3, SHP-2,and Shc"],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":228,"s":10,"t":24,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:28213513"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/28213513\">pubmed:28213513</a> Our finding that RUNX1 protein levels are dependent on FLT3-ITD signaling in AML cells and that, together, they synergize to generate AML. […]Our work demonstrated that Tyr phosphorylation within the ID region of RUNX1 is critical for its oncogenic potential,"],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":229,"s":10,"t":106,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16684964"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0002882"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16684964\">pubmed:16684964</a> Y599 was additionally found to interact with the protein tyrosine phosphatase SHP2 in a phosphorylation-dependent manner. As Y599F-Flt3-32D was unable to associate with and to phosphorylate SHP2 and since silencing of SHP2 in WT-Flt3-expressing cells mimicked the Y599F-Flt3 phenotype, we hypothesize that recruitment of SHP2 to pY599 contributes to FL-mediated Erk activation and proliferation."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":230,"s":10,"t":97,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:15574429"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0004760"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15574429\">pubmed:15574429</a> Furthermore, a small but reproducible growth/survival advantage was observed in both TF-1 and TF-1/ITD cells when SHP-1 expression was knocked down by RNAi. Taken together, these data provide the first evidence that suppression of SHP-1 by FLT3/ITD signaling may be another mechanism contributing to the transformation by FLT3/ITD mutations"],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates quantity"}},{"id":231,"s":10,"t":97,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:15574429"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15574429\">pubmed:15574429</a> Expression of FLT3/ITD induces down-regulation of SHP-1 expression and activity"],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates quantity by repression"}},{"id":232,"s":10,"t":95,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:18192505"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/18192505\">pubmed:18192505</a> Inhibition of FLT3/ITD leads to a small decrease in RAC1 activity"],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":233,"s":10,"t":50,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:17356133","pubmed:12796379"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["","Tyr694"],"sequence":["","LAKAVDGyVKPQIKQ"],"cell_data":["BTO:0001516","BTO:0002882"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["","gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12796379\">pubmed:12796379</a>  FLT3-ITDs induced a strong activation of STAT5. FLT3-ITD mutants induce an autophosphorylation of the receptor, interleukin 3-independent growth in Ba/F3 cells, and a strong STAT5 and mitogen-activated protein kinase (MAPK) activation. ","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/17356133\">pubmed:17356133</a> in vitro kinase assays revealed that STAT5 is a direct target of Flt3"],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":235,"s":10,"t":84,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:22438257"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/22438257\">pubmed:22438257</a> Taken together, the described findings supported the notion that FLT3 ITD causes reduced DEP-1 activity compared with cells expressing WT FLT3 rather than alterations in mRNA or protein levels."],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates activity"}},{"id":236,"s":10,"t":80,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:14982881"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0002181"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/14982881\">pubmed:14982881</a> We report here that the Flt3-ITD interferes with the transcriptional and biologic action of the PLZF transcriptional repressor. In the presence of Flt3-ITD, PLZF-SMRT interaction was reduced, transcriptional repression by PLZF was inhibited, and PLZF-mediated growth suppression of leukemia cells was partially blocked. Furthermore, overexpression of Flt3-ITD led to a partial relocalization of SMRT protein from the nucleus to the cytoplasm."],"direct":false,"i":"down-regulates activity"}},{"id":237,"s":10,"t":17,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:25477897"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/25477897\">pubmed:25477897</a> The three miR-29 family members in mouse bone marrow cells reduced the level of TET2 as well as its metabolic by-product, 5hmC "],"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":238,"s":10,"t":57,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:16266983","pubmed:14981546"],"mechanism":["","phosphorylation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["","BTO:0001516"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["","gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16266983\">pubmed:16266983</a> We show that the presence of Flt3-ITD constitutively activates Akt (PKB), a key serine-threonine kinase within the phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase pathway.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/14981546\">pubmed:14981546</a>  These data confirm previous findings that FLT3 receptors with ITD mutations efficiently trigger the activation of ERK, STAT5 and Akt in the absence of FL stimulation."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":240,"s":10,"t":58,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:30552988","pubmed:14981546"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["","miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/14981546\">pubmed:14981546</a>  These data confirm previous findings that FLT3 receptors with ITD mutations efficiently trigger the activation of ERK, STAT5 and Akt in the absence of FL stimulation.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/30552988\">pubmed:30552988</a> Oncogenic, constitutively active mutants of FLT3 are known to be expressed in acute myeloid leukemia and to correlate with poor prognosis. Activation of the receptor mediates cell survival, cell proliferation and differentiation of cells. Several of the signal transduction pathways downstream of FLT3 have been shown to include various members of the SRC family of kinases (SFKs). They are involved in regulating the activity of RAS/ERK pathways through the scaffolding protein GAB2 and the adaptor protein SHC."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":242,"s":10,"t":55,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:23246379"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0001516"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23246379\">pubmed:23246379</a> Grb10 transduces signal from FLT3 by direct interaction with p85 and Ba/F3-FLT3-ITD cells expressing Grb10 exhibits higher STAT5 activation.  These results suggest that Grb10 binds to both normal and oncogenic FLT3 and induces PI3K-Akt and STAT5 signaling pathways resulting in an enhanced proliferation, survival and colony formation of hematopoietic cells."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":243,"s":124,"t":125,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:25477897"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/25477897\">pubmed:25477897</a> Overexpression of miR-155 leads to the activation of the PI3K-Akt pathway through negative regulation of Src Homology 2 domain-containing Inositol-5-Phosphatase (SHIP1). "],"i":"up-regulates quantity"}},{"id":244,"s":12,"t":126,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:15340381"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15340381\">pubmed:15340381</a> P21 and p27 are key inhibitors of both cdk1 and cdk2."],"i":"down-regulates"}},{"id":245,"s":127,"t":15,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:23567751"],"mechanism":[""],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["miannu"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23567751\">pubmed:23567751</a> The mitochondrial pathway of apoptosis proceeds when the outer mitochondrial membrane (OMM) is compromised by the pro-apoptotic BCL-2 family members, BAK and BAX. Once activated, BAK and BAX form proteolipid pores in the OMM leading to mitochondrial outer membrane permeabilization (MOMP), and the release of inner membrane space proteins, such as cytochrome c, which promotes caspase activation."],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":246,"s":38,"t":128,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:9575217"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr705"],"sequence":["DPGSAAPyLKTKFIC"],"cell_data":["BTO:0000599"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9575217\">pubmed:9575217</a> Inactive cytoplasmic STATs are recruited to the activated receptor by docking of the STAT SH2 domain to selected receptor tyrosine phosphopeptides, where they are in turn phosphorylated on a single tyrosine by Jak kinases. Has been identified tyrosine 705 of Stat3 as the likely site of phosphorylation by Jak kinases during signal transduction."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":247,"s":38,"t":38,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:17027227","pubmed:20304997","pubmed:15143187","pubmed:19364823","pubmed:15121872","pubmed:9111318"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr813","Tyr637","Tyr221","Tyr972","Tyr1007","Tyr201"],"sequence":["KFGSLDTyLKKNKNC","VLPQDKEyYKVKEPG","EYLGTKRyIHRDLAT","IRAKIQDyHILTRKR","NSLFTPDyELLTEND","DQTPLAIyNSISYKT"],"cell_data":["BTO:0000298","BTO:0000007",""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":["","16705160:The effect of Ser523 on Jak2 function was independent of Tyr570-mediated inhibition."],"annotator":["","lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9111318\">pubmed:9111318</a>  Multiple autophosphorylation sites on Jak2, including Y1007 and Y1008. Activation of Jak2 catalytic activity requires phosphorylation of Y1007 in the kinase activation loop.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20304997\">pubmed:20304997</a>  Tyrosines 868, 966, and 972 in the kinase domain of jak2 are autophosphorylated and required for maximal jak2 kinase activity","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15143187\">pubmed:15143187</a> JAK2 is autophosphorylated on tyrosines 221 and 1007. tyrosines 221 and 570 in JAK2 may serve as regulatory sites in JAK2, with phosphorylation of tyrosine 221 increasing kinase activity and phosphorylation of tyrosine 570 decreasing kinase activity","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15121872\">pubmed:15121872</a>  Tyrosine 813 is a site of jak2 autophosphorylation critical for activation of jak2 by sh2-b betawe show that phosphorylation of tyrosine 813 is required for the sh2 domain-containing adapter protein sh2-b beta to bind jak2 and to enhance the activity of jak2 and stat5b.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/17027227\">pubmed:17027227</a>  Site of Jak2 tyrosine autophosphorylation; namely, tyrosine 201. Jak2 tyrosine residue 201 was the principal mediator of SHP-2 binding as conversion of this tyrosine residue to phenylalanine abolished this interaction","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/19364823\">pubmed:19364823</a>  Analysis of in vitro autophosphorylated jak2while cytokine receptor stimulation mediates the phosphorylation of both tyr317 and tyr637, these residues oppositely regulate jak2-dependent signaling: the mutation of tyr317 enhances jak2 function, suggesting a role for the phosphorylation of tyr317 in the inhibition of jak2. Conversely, mutation of tyr637 reduces jak2 signaling, suggesting a role for the phosphorylation of this residue in the activation of jak2."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":248,"s":38,"t":38,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:20304997","pubmed:15143187"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr868","Tyr966","Tyr221"],"sequence":["QICKGMEyLGTKRYI","GSVEMCRyDPLQDNT","IRAKIQDyHILTRKR"],"cell_data":["BTO:0000007"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15143187\">pubmed:15143187</a>  Autophosphorylation of jak2 on tyrosines 221 and 570 regulates its activity with phosphorylation of tyrosine 221 increasing kinase activity","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20304997\">pubmed:20304997</a>  Tyrosines 868, 966, and 972 in the kinase domain of jak2 are autophosphorylated and required for maximal jak2 kinase activity","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20304997\">pubmed:20304997</a> Tyrosines 868, 966, and 972 in the kinase domain of jak2 are autophosphorylated and required for maximal jak2 kinase activity"],"i":"up-regulates"}},{"id":256,"s":38,"t":38,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:9111318"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr1007"],"sequence":["VLPQDKEyYKVKEPG"],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9111318\">pubmed:9111318</a> Within the Jak2 kinase domain, there is a region that has considerable sequence homology to the regulatory region of the insulin receptor and contains two tyrosines, Y1007 and Y1008, that are potential regulatory sites.  Y1007 and Y1008 are sites of trans- or autophosphorylation in vivo and in in vitro kinase reactions. Mutation of Y1007, or both Y1007 and Y1008, to phenylalanine essentially eliminated kinase activity, whereas mutation of Y1008 to phenylalanine had no detectable effect on kinase activity"],"i":"unknown"}},{"id":257,"s":38,"t":38,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:19364823"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr317"],"sequence":["TEQDLQLyCDFPNII"],"cell_data":["BTO:0000007"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":["16705160:the phosphorylation of Jak2 on Ser523 inhibits Jak2 activity and represents a novel mechanism for the regulation of Jak2-dependent cytokine signaling."],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/19364823\">pubmed:19364823</a> Analysis of in vitro autophosphorylated jak2while cytokine receptor stimulation mediates the phosphorylation of both tyr317 and tyr637, these residues oppositely regulate jak2-dependent signaling: the mutation of tyr317 enhances jak2 function, suggesting a role for the phosphorylation of tyr317 in the inhibition of jak2. Conversely, mutation of tyr637 reduces jak2 signaling, suggesting a role for the phosphorylation of this residue in the activation of jak2."],"i":"down-regulates"}},{"id":258,"s":38,"t":38,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:21841788","pubmed:15143187"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr570","Ser523"],"sequence":["GVSDVPTsPTLQRPT","VRREVGDyGQLHETE"],"cell_data":["","BTO:0000007"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["","lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15143187\">pubmed:15143187</a> JAK2 is autophosphorylated on tyrosines 221 and 1007. tyrosines 221 and 570 in JAK2 may serve as regulatory sites in JAK2, with phosphorylation of tyrosine 221 increasing kinase activity and phosphorylation of tyrosine 570 decreasing kinase activity","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/21841788\">pubmed:21841788</a>  The jak2 jh2 domain functions as a negative regulator and is presumed to be a catalytically inactive pseudokinase, but the mechanism(s) for its inhibition of jak2 remains unknown. Here we show that jh2 is a dual-specificity protein kinase that phosphorylates two negative regulatory sites in jak2: ser523 and tyr570."],"i":"down-regulates activity"}},{"id":261,"s":38,"t":61,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:12370803"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["irozzo"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12370803\">pubmed:12370803</a> In this study, we show that Jak2 is involved in c-Myc induction by inducing c-MYC mRNA and protecting c-Myc protein from 26S proteasome-dependent degradation. These results indicate that c-Myc is a downstream target of activated Jak2 in Bcr-Abl positive cells. "],"i":"up-regulates quantity by stabilization"}},{"id":262,"s":38,"t":61,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:12370803"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["irozzo"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12370803\">pubmed:12370803</a> In this study, we show that Jak2 is involved in c-Myc induction by inducing c-MYC mRNA and protecting c-Myc protein from 26S proteasome-dependent degradation. These results indicate that c-Myc is a downstream target of activated Jak2 in Bcr-Abl positive cells. "],"direct":false,"i":"up-regulates quantity by expression"}},{"id":263,"s":38,"t":50,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:9575217"],"mechanism":["phosphorylation"],"residue":["Tyr694"],"sequence":["LAKAVDGyVKPQIKQ"],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":["gcesareni"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9575217\">pubmed:9575217</a> Our mutational analysis suggests that the Stat5 SH2 domain is essential for the interaction with Jak2 and that the kinase domain of Jak2 is sufficient for Jak2-Stat5 interaction. Therefore, the Ja