_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/18179858\">pubmed:18179858</a>  KIT mutations within the carboxy-terminal region of the cytoplasmic tyrosine kinase domain (TK2), such as KITD816V, stabilize the KIT activation loop conformation in its active form.Previous studies have demonstrated hyperactivation of p85α regulatory subunit of class IA phosphatidylinositol-3-kinase (PI3K) in cell lines expressing the activation loop mutant of KIT. Although p85α is hyperphosphorylated and constitutively bound to KITD814V in cell-line models."],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":379,"s":122,"t":55,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:23246379"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":["BTO:0001516"],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"annotator":[""],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/23246379\">pubmed:23246379</a> Grb10 transduces signal from FLT3 by direct interaction with p85 and Ba/F3-FLT3-ITD cells expressing Grb10 exhibits higher STAT5 activation"],"i":"up-regulates activity"}},{"id":380,"s":27,"t":59,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:19007744"],"mechanism":["binding"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":["Cytosolic p53"],"annotator":["lperfetto"],"sentence":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/19007744\">pubmed:19007744</a> Mechanistic insights into the mitochondrial function of wtp53 came when it was realized that mitochondrially translocated p53 interacts directly with members of the Bcl-2 family, which are central in governing the induction of mitochondrial outer membrane permeabilization. In response to stress, wtp53 interacts with and neutralizes the anti-apoptotic members Bcl-xL and Bcl-2. This interaction stimulates MOMP and subsequent apoptosis"],"i":"down-regulates activity"}},{"id":381,"s":27,"t":68,"v":{"citation":["pubmed:7958853"],"mechanism":["transcriptional regulation"],"residue":[""],"sequence":[""],"cell_data":[""],"tissue_data":[""],"notes":[""],"